= French president resigns

The independent president Alexandre Millerand won't appoint a leftist government and the leftist assembly won't collaborate with him, thus there is no other way but for him to resign from his post.

The French president is not electet directly but by both chambers, the Senate and the National Assembly.
  
The Radicals and Radical-Socialists have agreed to run Paul Painlevé (<span style="color: #FF6699;" class="tooltip-text" title="Republican-Socialist Party">**PRS**</span>), an anti-clerical <span style="color: #FF6699;" class="tooltip-text" title="A non-marxist socialist focused on achieving a "fair deal" between capital and labour">*Utopian Socialist*</span>. Yet some view him as too radical for the office of president and a counter candidacy has been proposed by Gaston Doumerge (<span style="color: #E0B0FF;" class="tooltip-text" title="Republican, Radical and Radical-Socialist Party">**PRRRS**</span>) who is more moderate.

- @frfr: Let's hope for the best...

@frfr
on-arrival: french_hos = "Doumerge"; french_hos_party = "PRRRS"
  
Doumerge wins!

Due to the high abstention rate in the first round, Painlevé was close to securing a majority of the votes. All the conservative parties threw their support behind Doumerge who secured a clear win in the end. Altogether this is still very good news for us...
















  
